# Without this, Git on Windows can check out shell scripts with CRLF line
# endings (depending on the cloning machine's core.autocrlf setting). A
# CRLF shebang line ("#!/bin/sh\r") is invalid inside a Linux container -
# the entrypoint then fails with a misleading "exec ...: no such file or
# directory" even though the file is right there (confirmed 2026-07-12:
# docker/postgres/entrypoint.sh crash-looped this way on a fresh Windows
# clone while the repo's own stored blob was already clean LF). Force LF
# for anything a Linux container executes or parses as a script, regardless
# of the cloning machine's git config.
* text=auto
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
